<title>USA: Butler authorizes 800,000 share buyback.</title>
<headline>Butler authorizes 800,000 share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Butler Manufacturing Co said Monday its board of directors authorized the repurchase of up to 800,000 shares of the company's common stock.</p>
<p>The buyback program replaces a September 1995 plan authorizing the repurchase of up to 500,000 shares, the company said. Under that plan, Butler repurchased 88,000 shares at an average cost of $29 a share. The company currently has 7.8 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The repurchased shares will be used for general corporate purposes, including the company's employee stock plans.</p>
<p>	  ((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
